      "result": {
        "ok": true,
        "tool": "read_evidence",
        "preview": "{\"evidence_id\":\"evidence-dcc8785967cf133ac2051340b1a30df69946049886673e385707e40db67e0375\",\"version\":1,\"content_hash\":\"sha256:2d5a4cc574db24e11629ccc5a268ef55b6a2e4bf752a1c0495dd10f05ce87703\",\"historical\":false,\"passages\":[{\"ref\":\"n1\",\"start\":0,\"end\":34,\"text\":\"---\\ntitle: Structured output\\n---\\n\\n\"},{\"ref\":\"n2\",\"start\":1176,\"end\":1516,\"text\":\"- **`ToolStrategy[StructuredResponseT]`**: Uses tool calling for structured output\\n- **`ProviderStrategy[StructuredResponseT]`**: Uses provider-native structured output\\n- **`type[StructuredResponseT]`**: Schema type - automatically selects best strategy based on model capabilities\\n- **`None`**: Structured output not explicitly requested\\n\\n\"},{\"ref\":\"n3\",\"start\":2869,\"end\":3092,\"text\":\"<Tip>\\nThis page covers structured output with agents using `createAgent`. To use structured output directly on a model (outside of agents), see [Models - Structured output](/oss/langchain/models#structured-output).\\n</Tip>\\n\\n\"},{\"ref\":\"n4\",\"start\":3705,\"end\":4095,\"text\":\"Controls how the agent returns structured data. You can provide a Zod schema, any [Standard Schema](https://standardschema.dev/)-compatible schema, or a JSON Schema object. By default, the agent uses a tool calling strategy, in which the output is created by an additional tool call. Certain models support native structured output, in which case the agent will use that strategy instead.\\n\\n\"},{\"ref\":\"n5\",\"start\":5160,\"end\":5417,\"text\":\"## Provider strategy\\n\\nSome model providers support structured output natively through their APIs (e.g. OpenAI, xAI (Grok), Gemini, Anthropic (Claude)). This is the most reliable method when available.\\n\\nTo use this strategy, configure a `ProviderStrategy`:\\n\\n\"},{\"ref\":\"n6\",\"start\":13506,\"end\":13660,\"text\":\"Provider-native structured output provides high reliability and strict validation because the model provider enforces the schema. Use it when available.\\n\\n\"},{\"ref\":\"n7\",\"start\":14373,\"end\":14399,\"text\":\"## Tool calling strategy\\n\\n\"}],\"selection\":{\"strategy\":\"query\",\"body_length\":44432,\"omitted\":true,\"found\":true,\"reason\":\"preview_budget_omitted\"}}",
        "evidence_ids": []
      },
      "research_findings": []
    }
